    "block.qtcraft.signal_dropper": "Signal Dropper",
    "block.qtcraft.signal_hopper.description": "Moves items: every eight ticks it passes one item into the container its spout points at and takes one from the container above it, or collects items lying in its bowl or on a block above it that does not fill its cell (a slab, a carpet, farmland). Any signal locks it.",
    "block.qtcraft.signal_comparator.description": "Puts out the strength from its back, or what it reads from a container (how full it is) or another readable block behind it, also through one block. In compare mode a stronger side input switches it off, in subtract mode it is taken off (use it to change the mode).",
    "block.qtcraft.signal_observer.description": "Watches the block its face looks at and sends a short pulse out of its back when that block changes.",
    "block.qtcraft.signal_dispenser.description": "On a rising signal ejects one item from a random slot: pours and takes liquids with buckets, puts armour on a player or armour stand in front and throws anything else out, also in front of a container. Seeds are thrown, not planted.",
    "block.qtcraft.signal_dropper.description": "On a rising signal throws one item from a random slot out of its front, or puts it into a container in front.",
